{
  "requirement": "The documented coverage overview presents a compact table of source\nfiles with coverage annotations and links to their explanations.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has three parts. The overview must be a compact table. It must list source files with coverage annotations. It must link to the explanations for those files.\n\n**Main test:** `src/execution_coverage/book.rs#mod[tests]/fn[documented_items_are_counted_once_with_browsable_directory_and_file_groups]` builds a multi-file fixture and renders the overview through `populate` and the helper `map_html`. It checks each part:\n- **Compact:** `!html.contains(\"\\n\\n\")` checks that the markup has no blank lines. The test also checks that the root file row is not hidden and is not inside a `<details>` group.\n- **Files with annotations:** the row for each documented file (`code.rs`, `src/direct.rs`, `src/deep/nested.rs`) must contain `</button></td><td>{expected_count}</td>`. The expected counts are 2, 2 and 1. The test also asserts the total \"7 documented source items carrying coverage annotations\".\n- **Files without annotations:** `src/pass.rs` must not appear, so only annotated files are listed.\n- **Links to explanations:** each row's card must contain an `href` to the generated notes page path, plus per-ordinal `#coverage-note-N` anchors. The test checks that the notes chapter exists with that path and contains the matching `id=\"coverage-note-N\"` anchors. It also checks that the explanation text and the `file:line #selector` locations appear.\n- **Directory placement:** the `src/deep`, `vendor` and `docs_only` files are covered through the `assert_directory_contents` and `directory_group` helpers.\n\n**Escaping test:** `fn[documented_paths_and_explanations_escape_html]` checks that a path and an explanation containing HTML special characters are escaped in the table output.\n\n**Reviewed helpers:** `map_html`, `file_card`, `directory_group` and `fixture` are reached from the marked tests. They scope the assertions to the real rendered section and cards.\n\nI found no plausible violation that these tests would accept. A missing or wrong count would fail the count assertions. A missing or wrong link would fail the href and anchor assertions. An unescaped path would fail the escaping test.",
